Adsorption Science and Technology — Sourav Mondal, IIT Kharagpur (@gas-adsorption-course: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gas-sources) { r_4P0F5BH9XEAJQPGJ0CTTJ76XM5
Sourav Mondal, IIT Kharagpur. *Adsorption Science and Technology: Fundamentals and Applications*, NPTEL 103105461. [Official course](https://www.nptel.ac.in/courses/103105461), [complete syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/103105461.pdf).

Study the complete eight-week course. Equilibrium, multicomponent isotherms and kinetics lead into pore/surface inference, film and particle transport, fixed-bed models, mass-transfer zones, multiscale modeling and pressure-swing adsorption. Chromatography and ion exchange provide useful comparisons of separation principles. Work the published examples and derive the assumptions behind simplified bed models.

The official identity and full two-page syllabus were inspected on 30 October 2026. The syllabus locates fixed-bed and PSA work in weeks 5–6. Video playback, all assessments and software execution were not verified. The course's treatment of an oxygen-concentrator example is a specific application, not qualification of an independently designed medical device.

Preserve actual course-run and component rights. Authorized free study does not establish an unrestricted redistribution licence. All lecture media and supplementary material remain external references.

